@startuml 04-event-flow
title NATS Subject Map — publishers and subscribers

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor<<svc>>     #E3F2FD
  BackgroundColor<<subject>> #FFF8E1
  BorderColor                #455A64
}

rectangle "CatalogueService" <<svc>> as catalogue
rectangle "AuctionsService"  <<svc>> as auctions
rectangle "WalletService"    <<svc>> as wallet
rectangle "OrdersService"    <<svc>> as orders

queue "product.>"  <<subject>> as s_product
queue "auction.>"  <<subject>> as s_auction
queue "wallet.>"   <<subject>> as s_wallet
queue "order.>"    <<subject>> as s_order

' Publishers
catalogue --> s_product : product.created\nproduct.updated\nproduct.deleted
auctions  --> s_auction : auction.created\nbid.placed\nauction.accepted\nauction.closed
wallet    --> s_wallet  : wallet.debited\nwallet.refunded
orders    --> s_order   : order.created\norder.failed

' Subscribers
s_product --> auctions  : enrich local cache
s_auction --> catalogue : lock / unlock product
s_auction --> wallet    : auction.accepted → debit
s_wallet  --> orders    : wallet.debited → create order
s_order   --> auctions  : order.created → close
s_order   --> wallet    : order.failed → refund

note bottom of s_auction
  NATS subjects use dot-separated hierarchy.
  Wildcards: "*" matches one token, ">" matches the rest.
  A single subscriber on "auction.>" receives every auction.* message.
  Payload: plain JSON (no schema registry needed).
end note

@enduml
